            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.32183/2611.32183v1/stage1.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:Overview of the two training stages.Stage 1 (top)uses seven instruction-free visual pretext tasks to practice producing and reading intermediate images.Stage 2 (bottom)uses question-driven instruction tuning to teach the model to use image content to advance reasoning across basic visual perception, static spatial understanding, and mental world modeling.",
