                "caption": "Figure 2:Instruct-180K construction pipelines.The pipelines are grouped into three levels of vision-centric reasoning: basic visual perception, static spatial understanding, and mental world modeling. Each panel shows how one pipeline constructs the intermediate visual state used in an interleaved reasoning example, such as a localized crop, a reordered view, a depth map, an edited object state, or a synthesized viewpoint. Full details are provided in AppendixD.",
