                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.32183/2611.32183v1/figures/topdown_candidate_failures.png",
                "caption": "Figure 9:Representative failures of off-the-shelf and fine-tuned\ncandidates on real scenes.Top:a SAM3D-based composite of\nthe small objects on the bed yields a generic synthetic-looking\nplatform, and a Qwen-Edit model further fine-tuned (LoRA + SFT) on\nsynthetic top-down pairs only resamples a different angle of that\nfabricated scene rather than depicting the actual input.Bottom:given the prompt “turn the camera to a top-down\nview”, Qwen-Edit, Nano-Banana-Pro, and a multi-angle Qwen-Edit\nfine-tune each return a wrong camera angle and drift in object\norientation. The picture is consistent across many scenes.",
